From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominik Weber <doweb85@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:00:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 21/27] byteplan: sparse prefill attention on simdgroup MMA,
 narrow-row dispatch, 64-row matmul tiles

kernel_flash_attn_ext_sparse: a large sparse batch (QSA prefill) runs all heads of a KV group per threadgroup over the
query's index list, K/V fragments loaded straight from the gathered cache rows into the simdgroup matrices; 3x faster
than one vec threadgroup per query and head. Rounding changes; KL against one-row decoding is unchanged (0.00213 vs
0.00202 +- 0.00013, top-1 98.91 vs 98.90 %). BYTEPLAN_FA_SPARSE_MMA_OFF=1 keeps the vec path.
Unary, get_rows and repeat put several narrow rows into one threadgroup instead of a threadgroup of 1-4 threads per
row (same element math). Dense mul_mm takes 64 src1 rows per threadgroup for batches of 512+ rows, so every
dequantized weight tile serves twice the rows (same MMA sequence per element).
